ook and waits for either a [Actual] disclosure of high-value licensing economics or a materially lower price.\n\n---\n\n*Everything above is the work of the integrated analysis engine. Where the pack could not deliver a fact or a search could not retrieve it, the deficiency is stated [Unconfirmed] rather than assumed \u2014 and the uncertainty is carried through the scenario probabilities and position sizes.*"}, {"sample": 2, "iv": 115.0, "plausible": true, "reasons": [], "flags": [], "truncated": false, "secs": 381, "report": "```text\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 RS2 v2.0 INTEGRATED INVESTMENT ANALYSIS \u2014 SPHERE ENTERTAINMENT CO. (SPHR)\n\u25a0 T0: 2026-08-24 | Price: $158.36 | Market Cap: $5.687B | Shares: 35.913M\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 0. ANALYSIS OVERVIEW\n\n- Analyzing SPHR at T0 price $158.36 (Tier 2 [Actual], vendor quote).\n- Data integrity: FY2020 `shares_diluted` value of 24,017 is a provable scale corruption and was EXCLUDED. No other full-series corruption was identified.\n- Critical data gaps: (i) No segment revenue/margin detail in the XBRL extract; (ii) capex missing for FY2023\u2013FY2025, making the TTM capex of $1.005B impossible to decompose; (iii) debt-component overlap unknown; (iv) MSG Networks debt is non-recourse to the parent (Sportico, 2025 [Estimate]) but remains on the consolidated balance sheet.\n- Valuation engine: Engine 4 (Expectation-Driven / Option-Led) because SPHR's equity value is dominated by the optionality of international Sphere expansion (Abu Dhabi, National Harbor, and other markets), with a single-asset Las Vegas core and a declining RSN segment. Transition check: SPHR partly meets \"Hybrid\" criteria (core Las Vegas revenue >50% of total, content/platform monetization beginning), but the future value is disproportionately from unbuilt, unconsolidated venues; therefore Engine 4 is primary, with a Sum-of-Parts discipline applied.\n- Model confidence: LOW. Tiers 4-5 inputs (international fee economics, probability of venue replication, true maintenance capex) drive the result and are not verifiable from the data pack.\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 1. MACRO CONTEXT\n\n- 10-Year Treasury: 4.70% at 2026-08-24 (FRED [Actual]); direction: flat-to-slightly-up over recent months.\n- Fed policy target: 3.50%\u20133.75%, unchanged at the July 2026 meeting (Trading Economics [Actual]); market pricing a gradual move toward ~3.8% (StreetStats [Estimate]).\n- Dollar Index: [Unconfirmed] \u2014 not retrieved before the research budget expired; treated as neutral.\n- Inflation: [Estimate] core PCE around 2.5%\u20133.0% with residual services pressure; no confirmed datapoint in the pack.\n- Credit spreads: [Unconfirmed] \u2014 assumed around long-term averages, but flagged unverified.\n- Regime probabilities:\n    - Goldilocks (low rates + growth): 20%\n    - Reflation (high rates + growth): 45%\n    - Stagflation (high rates + low growth): 20%\n    - Recession (low rates + low growth): 15%\n- Macro sensitivity (each -3 to +3):\n    - Interest rate sensitivity: -2 (long-duration entertainment asset, consumer discretionary)\n    - Dollar sensitivity: -1 (some inbound tourism at Las Vegas venue)\n    - Liquidity sensitivity: -2 (heavy capital intensity; depends on capital markets