\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 3. VALUATION\n----------------------------------------------------------------\nEngine selection: Product-Platform Hybrid (Engine 3) with a reality check from Engine 4 (Expectation/Reverse DCF). The \u201cplatform\u201d is the Sphere brand/content/licensing system; the core is the Vegas venue and MSG Networks.\n\n3-A. Segments and Base-Case Build\nEstimated current split (TTM):\n- Las Vegas Sphere revenue: ~$0.95B [Estimate from Q4 2025 Sphere revenue $274.2M [Actual] and Q2 2026 Sphere revenue $226.4M [Actual]]\n- MSG Networks revenue: ~$0.40B [Estimate from Q2 2026 segment revenue $87.3M, -18.5% YoY [Actual]]\n- Corporate/other: ~$0.01B\n\nBase-case forecast (my assumptions, not guidance):\n| FY | Revenue $B | AOI $B | AOI% | Content/Maint Capex $B | Cash Tax $B | FCFF $B |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2026E | 1.40 | 0.20 | 14% | 0.30 | 0.00 | -0.10 |\n| 2027E | 1.45 | 0.23 | 16% | 0.20 | 0.00 | 0.03 |\n| 2028E | 1.50 | 0.26 | 17% | 0.15 | 0.00 | 0.11 |\n| 2029E | 1.55 | 0.28 | 18% | 0.15 | 0.00 | 0.13 |\n| 2030E | 1.65 | 0.31 | 19% | 0.15 | 0.00 | 0.16 |\n| 2031E | 1.75 | 0.35 | 20% | 0.15 | 0.00 | 0.20 |\n| 2032E | 1.90 | 0.40 | 21% | 0.15 | 0.00 | 0.25 |\n| 2033E | 2.05 | 0.45 | 22% | 0.15 | 0.01 | 0.29 |\n| 2034E | 2.20 | 0.51 | 23% | 0.15 | 0.02 | 0.34 |\n| 2035E | 2.35 | 0.56 | 24% | 0.15 | 0.03 | 0.38 |\n\nForecast driver sourcing:\n- Revenue growth: no multi-year company guidance exists beyond \u201csubstantial growth\u201d [Actual \u2014 management excerpt from Q2 2026 call]. The pack explicitly lacks analyst Q&A where capex guidance is usually pinned down. 2027+ growth is my assumption: LV Sphere revenue grows +3\u20135% from pricing, MSG Networks declines -15%/yr, and two expansions (Abu Dhabi 2030, National Harbor 2032) contribute license/management fees starting at $25M, growing to ~$50M each by 2035. [Assumption]\n- AOI margin: Q4 2025 Sphere segment AOI margin was 32.6% [Actual], but consolidated includes negative networks/corporate and content ramp; 24% by 2035 is a reasonable long-term blended margin if two fee-based venues open. [Assumption]\n- Capex: TTM capex is $1.005B [Actual]. This is not a steady-state number; it includes one-time content/production, land/development, and possibly Abu Dhabi-related advance. My base forecast normalises to $0.15B/yr maintenance/content spend by 2028. If it instead stays at $0.30B+, intrinsic value is below the central estimate. [Assumption]\n- D&A is irrelevant to FCFF but relevant to taxes; I assumed NOLs shield taxes until ~2033. [Assumption]\n\n3-B. Discount Rate Derivation\n- Risk-free: 10Y UST = 4.71% [Actual]\n- Beta: 1.625 [Aggregator \u2014 vendor window/benchmark unstated]\n- ERP: 5.0% [Assumption]\n- Cost of equity = 4.71% + 1.625 \u00d7 5.0% = 12.84%\n- Cost of debt: 8% [Estimate \u2014 no current coupon retrieved], after-tax at 21% = 6.3%\n- Weights: Equity 92.8%, Debt 7.2% (EV $6.127B, net debt $0.440B)\n- WACC = 0.928 \u00d7 12.84% + 0.072 \u00d7 6.3% = 12.4%. Use 12%. [Estimate]\n\n3-C. Base-Case DCF\nPV of explicit FCFF: $0.76B [Arithmetic]\nTerminal FCFF (2035): $0.38B; g=3%; TV = $0.38 \u00d7 1.03 / (0.12\u22120.03) = $4.35B; PV of TV = $1.40B.\nEV = $2.16B.\nEquity = $2.16B \u2212 $0.44B net debt = $1.72B.\nPer share = $1.72B / 35.913M = ~$48.\n\n3-D. Scenario Valuation (see Section 4 for probabilities)\n- Bear: ~$18/share\n- Base: ~$48/share\n- Bull: ~$120/share\n- Blue-sky: ~$240/share\nCentral expected value = 25%\u00d718 + 45%\u00d748 + 25%\u00d7120 + 5%\u00d7240 = $68 [Arithmetic/Assumption].\n\n3-E. Reverse DCF / Market-Implied Expectations\nAt the current EV of $6.13B, with the explicit FCF PV above of ~$0.76B, the terminal value needed is $5.37B PV, i.e. ~$16.7B terminal value at 2035, requiring ~$1.5B of FCFF in 2035 (WACC 12%, g=3%).\n- That implies adjusted EBITDA/AOI of roughly $1.9B after maintenance capex and taxes.\n- To get there SPHR would need ~10 mature Spheres each contributing $150\u2013200M of AOI, or a far larger number of licensed venues. At a lower 10% WACC, required 2035 FCFF is still ~$0.9B, i.e. 5\u20137 successful venues with high fee economics.\n\n3-F. Tornado Sensitivity (Top 3)\n1. WACC: 10% vs 12% moves central value ~30\u201350% higher.\n2. Number of additional Spheres and fee income per Sphere: 0 to 10 new venues swings value from $18 to $240.\n3. Normalized content/maintenance capex: $100M vs $300M changes value by roughly \u00b140%.\n\nConclusion: The current price is a blue-sky-derived number, not a base-case number.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n- Competitive response: If Sphere Abu Dhabi is a hit, local governments will demand similar venues, but competitors (Live Nation, IMAX, Disney, regional operators) can copy the \u201cimmersive venue\u201d concept once patents/licences expire. Competitive counter-move: -2 [Estimate].\n- Reflexivity: High stock price helps SPHR attract talent via SBC and gives credibility with governments; low stock price would impair the expansion story and make third-party financing harder. Positive reflexivity is currently helping, but it is fragile. [Estimate]\n- Customer evolution: Early adopter demand in Las Vegas was enormous; mainstream demand depends on content depth. Content production is the bottleneck: each new experience is expensive and slow. LTV/CAC is still unproven because repeat-visit rates are not disclosed. [Unconfirmed]\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 4. SCENARIOS (BAYESIAN)\n----------------------------------------------------------------\nPrior: Platform-transition success base rate 20\u201330% [Section 1.5].\nUpdate from actuals: Vegas AOI positive; Abu Dhabi construction started; National Harbor is still \u201cexpected to complete\u201d third-party financing [Actual \u2014 management]. The evidence supports a base-case but not a blue-sky prior.\n\nScenario probabilities and values:\n- Bear (25%): No additional funded Spheres; Vegas matures with AOI $250M; Networks fades to zero; FCF stays thin. Value ~$18.\n- Base (45%): Abu Dhabi opens 2030, National Harbor 2032; each contributes $25\u201350M of high-margin fee income by 2035; Vegas AOI $300M; total 2035 FCFF ~$380M. Value ~$48.\n- Bull (25%): Five new Spheres by 2035, each contributing $50M+ EBITDA; Vegas AOI $350M; FCFF ~$500M by 2035. Value ~$120.\n- Blue-sky (5%): Ten+ Spheres by 2035; AOI $1.2B; FCFF ~$900M. Value ~$240.\n\nBayesian check: Bull+Blue-sky = 30%, at the top of base rate. Price requires total >70% probability on outperformance, which fails the 2.0x base-rate red flag.\n\nExpected price = $68. Margin of Safety = ($68 \u2212 $158.36) / $68 = -133% relative to IV? Better: MoS = (IV \u2212 Price)/IV = (68\u2212158)/68 = -1.32 \u2192 none. Strictly MoS = (IV \u2212 Price)/Price = -57%. Use that: Expected return = -57% from current price.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 4.5. TIME HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n- Market-implied horizon: >10 years; the market is paying for a 5\u201310 venue global network.\n- My reliable 3\u20135 year horizon: no new venue generates meaningful revenue before 2029/2030; only one venue is operating.\n- Spread: ~5 years of unrealistically early optionality. This is not a positive arbitrage; it is negative asymmetry. The near years cannot validate the long-dated story, so the position depends entirely on 2030+ execution under a 12% discount rate.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 5. CONVICTION & POSITION SIZING\n----------------------------------------------------------------\nConviction Score:\n- Business quality: 2/3 (narrow moat, concerning financials)\n- Valuation attractiveness: 0/3 (price 2.3x central IV)\n- Macro alignment: 1/3 (late-cycle, liquidity-sensitive)\n- Thesis clarity: 2/3 (clear KPIs, but unproven)\n- Execution traceability: 1/3 (no detailed capex plan available)\nTotal: 6/15 \u2192 Low conviction.\nMacro headwind: -0.5 step \u2192 Effective conviction: Low.\nPosition cap: 0\u20132% for a speculative long; our computed fair value makes the correct long weight 0%.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550